            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_INITIAL_INFO_DISPLAYS",
          "id": "1769732738347",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769732738349_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Business Content with Media. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.  \nDATA: {{$context.$nodes.RETURN_CONTENTS.$output.result}}  \n\nDIRECTIVE:  \nYour sole purpose is to transform input data into a valid oraInfoDisplay XML block using the multiRecordWidget.  \n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:  \n1.  title: Generate a concise, relevant headline reflecting the dataset’s business value or subject.  \n2.  description: Generate a short summary describing the displayed records, highlighting any video content and access to media.  \n\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:  \n3.  For the multiRecordWidget:  \n    - Dynamically generate the cols array using all unique property names in the dataset.  \n    - Do not generate any cols which are not present in the key of the dataset\n    - Do not include \"URL\" or \"Video Link\" or \"Media Link\" or \"File Name\" or \"Attachment Description\" or \"Url\" columns in the cols array.\n    - Do not create any column with badge. Remove that column from the list\n    - Column headers must use initial capital letters (e.g., \"Title\", \"Feature\", \"Product Name\", \"Transcript\").  \n    - Exclude metadata, locale, or other system fields.  \n    - For each row:  \n        - Place a clickable View Content link or button only when the corresponding property is a valid media/video URL.  \n        - When View Content is rendered, ensure it triggers ora.Invoke(\"showMedia\", \"<url>\") with <url> replaced by the exact URL from the data.  \n        - For text fields such as Oracle Positioning and Report Summary, if the text exceeds 20 words or 200 characters, summarize the content into a clear, professional paragraph of 2 to 3 sentences that highlights the main points.  \n        - For other columns, display their values as provided if 20 words or fewer and under 200 characters; otherwise, summarize into a single clear, professional sentence.  \n        - Omit empty or undefined values from cells.  \n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
